  "sampling": "Four A/A pairs of the same accepted R109 ELF, followed by six permutations of the three exact ELFs at each connection count. Fresh daemon for every run, CPU1 daemon/CPU0 caller. Fixed 44 samples, no optional extension.",
  "analysis": "Descriptive paired counts per validated send, report every raw sample and A/A spread. No IID confidence claim for the balanced permutation cycle, no equivalence test or acceptance based on Oracle CPU.",
  "decision": "Only this normalized cohort can estimate the net code-change effect in its stated startup configuration. If R111 instruction overhead versus R109 persists, do not make another control-flow variant. R110-A memory failure remains; no final acceptance from counters.",
  "boundaries": "Enable ACK after warmup before the three clock reads; disable ACK after the loop and the three clock reads. No per-request instrumentation. Final callback validates delivery; bounded trailing daemon work can straddle the CPU-clock/disable boundary. Counts include this boundary overhead and are divided by 50000.",
  "sources": [
    "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/perf-stat.1.html",
    "https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.17/tools/perf/util/evlist.c#L2078",
    "https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.17/tools/perf/util/evlist.h#L404"
  ],
